From: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: accept the bridge MAC on
 routed egress

A routed flow offered by the flowtable rewrites the ethernet source to
the address of the device the route resolves through. Behind a software
bridge that device is the bridge, and a bridge does not rewrite the
source of frames it forwards, so such a flow egresses a member port
carrying the bridge address. The egress sanity check only accepted the
member address and declined every routed flow (the reply direction on
this board, both directions of routed IPv6), with hardware entries
never installed.

Accept the address of the egress device master as well. DSA setups are
unaffected: a conduit and its user ports share one address, so the
master comparison was already true there.

Measured on TP-Link Archer BE800 (IPQ9574, non-DSA ports under a
software bridge): routed IPv6 now offloads both directions at 2.32
Gbit/s with the CPU port seeing 226 packets per 15 s transfer (was:
line rate through the CPU, flows declined "eth mangle src ... !=
egress ... mac"); IPv4 NAT unchanged (9 CPU packets per transfer).

Signed-off-by: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-02 07:33:49.570001752 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-02 07:33:49.570001752 +0000
@@ -940,6 +940,28 @@
 	return true;
 }
 
+// Routed traffic egressing a bridge member keeps the bridge MAC as
+// source (a bridge does not rewrite it), so the valid egress source MAC
+// is the member address or that of its master. This runs from the
+// nf_flow_table offload workqueue (no RTNL held), so the upper-device
+// lookup must use the RCU variant.
+static bool ppe_offload_egress_mac_matches(const u8 *mac,
+					    struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	struct net_device *master;
+	bool match;
+
+	if (ether_addr_equal(mac, dev->dev_addr))
+		return true;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	master = netdev_master_upper_dev_get_rcu(dev);
+	match = master && ether_addr_equal(mac, master->dev_addr);
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	return match;
+}
+
 static int ppe_offload_flow_replace(struct net_device *netdev,
 				     struct ppe_offload_priv *priv,
 				     struct flow_cls_offload *cls)
@@ -1451,7 +1472,7 @@
 	 * Behind a DSA user port that is the conduit's MAC, which its
 	 * user ports and (by default) their bridge inherit.
 	 */
-	if (!ether_addr_equal(eth.bytes + ETH_ALEN, egress.dev->dev_addr))
+	if (!ppe_offload_egress_mac_matches(eth.bytes + ETH_ALEN, egress.dev))
 		return ppe_offload_decline("eth mangle src %pM != egress %s mac %pM",
 					    eth.bytes + ETH_ALEN, netdev_name(egress.dev),
 					    egress.dev->dev_addr);
